{
  "name": "LOW-VIX armed trend continuation \u2014 ADX-confirmed strong-trend ride",
  "rationale": "Thesis: a strong directional trend (ADX gt adx_floor, BOUNDED) is most exploitable when macro vol is calm (VIX lt vix_ceiling) \u2014 low-VIX regimes give ADX trends room to run without macro-shock reversals. Require positive momentum (ret_Nd gt mom_floor) so direction is up, not just trendy. Ride until ADX decays below adx_exit (trend exhaustion) or risk/time stops. Disconfirmer 1 (is the low-VIX cap load-bearing?): the identical ADX-strong-trend long with NO VIX cap is in the cohort \u2014 if it matches the deflated Sharpe, the calm arm adds nothing and this is plain ADX trend-following. Disconfirmer 2 (is ADX load-bearing?): a low-VIX + momentum-only sibling with no ADX gate is in the cohort \u2014 if it matches, ADX adds no edge. Disconfirmer 3 (holdout): purged+embargoed recent slice must stay positive.",
  "catalyst": "VIX calm AND ADX strong-trend AND positive momentum",
